{"record": "turn", "turn": 4, "seconds": 6.705, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["thinking", "tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 2322}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2322, "cache_read_input_tokens": 8613, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 1034, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_013NBphaXB2oYpSkktuuCQDc", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "No. The two analyses use different thresholds and profile different nuisance parameters. The dSph gamma-ray limit is an approximate one-sided 95% CL upper limit, set where 2[ln L_max − ln L] = 2.71 (a TS drop of 2.71). It profiles over the individual dwarfs' J-factors, using a Gaussian prior in log10 s with J = sJ0 and s profiled over log10 s in [−3, 3]. The AMS-02 antiproton limit is the upper endpoint of the ΔQ ≤ 3.84 region, where Q = −2 ln L. The paper calls 3.84 the nominal one-parameter 95% interval threshold and says it differs from the one-sided 2.71 prescription. It profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, using a Gaussian penalty in log10 L centred on 4.96 kpc with σ = 0.197, profiled over 1–12 kpc.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261120T075137Z_dev-02_staged_da83", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "No. The two analyses use different thresholds and profile different nuisance parameters. The dSph gamma-ray limit is an approximate one-sided 95% CL upper limit, set where 2[ln L_max − ln L] = 2.71 (a TS drop of 2.71). It profiles over the individual dwarfs' J-factors, using a Gaussian prior in log10 s with J = sJ0 and s profiled over log10 s in [−3, 3]. The AMS-02 antiproton limit is the upper endpoint of the ΔQ ≤ 3.84 region, where Q = −2 ln L. The paper calls 3.84 the nominal one-parameter 95% interval threshold and says it differs from the one-sided 2.71 prescription. It profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, using a Gaussian penalty in log10 L centred on 4.96 kpc with σ = 0.197, profiled over 1–12 kpc.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}]}, "turns": 4, "seconds": 12.39, "tool_calls": 4, "tool_result_chars": 19377, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1353, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2322, "cache_read_input_tokens": 23044, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-20T07:51:50+00:00"}
